Why GPL-3.0 instead of MIT: the goal for this project is to stay free and
open forever. MIT would technically allow someone to take this code, add
ads or a paywall, and ship it as a closed-source app under a different
name — exactly the kind of app this project exists as an alternative to.
GPL-3.0's copyleft requirement means any distributed derivative work must
also stay open source under GPL-3.0, closing that loophole.
